---
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const install = `pnpm add -D @wesflo/vite-plugin-local-mock-api
pnpm add @wesflo/wf-vite-mock-proxy`;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<DocsLayout
    title="Overview"
    description="Local mock responses, selectable scenarios, and per-endpoint API passthrough for Vite."
    activePath="/"
>
    <article>
        <p class="kicker">Develop against the response you need</p>
        <h1>Local API mocks without an all-or-nothing switch.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            Serve realistic mock files from Vite, select scenarios in the browser, and pass individual endpoints through
            to a development API without removing the plugin from your configuration.
        </p>

        <Code code={install} label="terminal" />

        <div class="cards">
            <a class="card" href={`${base}/getting-started/`}>
                <strong>Get started →</strong>
                <span>Add the plugin, create a mock file, and make your first request.</span>
            </a>
            <a class="card" href={`${base}/proxy-panel/`}>
                <strong>Use the proxy panel →</strong>
                <span>Switch scenarios and bypass all mocks or a single endpoint.</span>
            </a>
            <a class="card" href={`${base}/configuration/`}>
                <strong>Configure the plugin →</strong>
                <span>Understand resolution rules, manifest fields, and plugin options.</span>
            </a>
            <a class="card" href={`${base}/playground/`}>
                <strong>Open the playground guide →</strong>
                <span>Exercise the panel and plugin together in a small micro frontend.</span>
            </a>
        </div>

        <h2>Three focused packages</h2>
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@wesflo/vite-plugin-local-mock-api</code></td>
                    <td>Vite development-server middleware for local files, scenarios, status codes, and delays.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@wesflo/wf-vite-mock-proxy</code></td>
                    <td>Embeddable Web Component that manages scenario and bypass cookies.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@wesflo/local-mock-api-utils</code></td>
                    <td>Shared cookie helpers and the fixed manifest route used by server and browser packages.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>How requests flow</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>The Vite middleware checks whether the request is inside the configured API prefix.</li>
            <li>A bypass cookie can send the request to the next middleware or configured Vite proxy.</li>
            <li>A selected manifest scenario can define a response file, status code, and delay.</li>
            <li>Without a selected scenario, the plugin resolves method-specific and generic mock files.</li>
        </ol>
    </article>
</DocsLayout>
